  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday night through next Thursday)\nIssued at 1021 PM CDT Thu Oct 1 2026\n\nThe upper level shear axis will dip farther to the south on Saturday \npushing precipitation chances farther south. Weak large scale ascent \nwill continue to be present mostly over the Rolling Plains. In \naddition, weak instability may develop early in the morning on \nSaturday bringing at least a slight chance of thunder to the Rolling \nPlains. Cooler air will receive a reinforcing shot of cooler air on \nSunday with a return to surface lee troughing on Monday. A period of \ndry weather and increasing temperatures is expected beginning in the \nsecond half of the weekend through at least the middle of next week. \nUpper level ridging will build over the four corners this weekend \ninto early next week but will become suppressed by the middle of \nnext week.",
